# MissAV Scraper API - Configuration

## Server Configuration
PORT=3000
VERBOSE=true

## Scraper Backend Configuration
# Choose which backend to use for fetching pages from missav.ws
# Options: direct, scrapfly, scraperapi, flaresolverr
#   - direct:      Direct HTTP requests (will NOT work if Cloudflare is blocking)
#   - scrapfly:    Uses Scrapfly.io API (recommended - free tier available)
#   - scraperapi:  Uses ScraperAPI.com (free tier available)
#   - flaresolverr: Uses self-hosted FlareSolverr proxy
SCRAPER_BACKEND=direct

## Scrapfly (https://scrapfly.io)
# Sign up for a free account to get your API key (1,000 free credits)
SCRAPFLY_API_KEY=your_scrapfly_api_key_here

## ScraperAPI (https://scraperapi.com)
# Sign up for a free account to get your API key (1,000 free API credits)
SCRAPERAPI_API_KEY=your_scraperapi_api_key_here

## FlareSolverr (Self-hosted — recommended for Vercel + Railway)
# Deploy FlareSolverr on Railway (free tier) and set the URL here.
# 1. Go to https://railway.app/new → "Deploy from Image"
# 2. Enter: flaresolverr/flaresolverr
# 3. Go to Settings → Networking → Generate Domain
# 4. Copy the URL (e.g., https://your-service.up.railway.app)
# 5. Set it below and add /v1 at the end
#
# Docker (local): docker run -d --name flaresolverr -p 8191:8191 flaresolverr/flaresolverr
FLARESOLVERR_URL=http://localhost:8191/v1
